# Work-rig snapshot (nested git repo, branch quarantine-work-dump-* pushed to origin).
# Its engine-split architecture + WS1/WS2 research were adopted onto main 2026-07-01
# (see CHANGELOG). Kept locally as a reference for the remaining WS3-WS6 items; safe to
# delete once those are ported. Ignored so it never gets committed into the outer repo.
# Both spellings: the drop historically arrived under the pre-rename name.
scythe/
zerobreach/

# Same work-rig-drop pattern, 2026-08-18: an untracked zerobreach-main/ folder appeared
# containing ONLY a Tauri native-app rewrite's Rust build cache (no source — no Cargo.toml,
# no .rs files) plus two real client scan-report HTML files. No source code was ever found
# for the native-app rewrite; it's a planned future engine replacement, not yet started here.
# Contents archived to _archive/zerobreach-main-dump/ (reports/ already caught by the
# global "reports/" rule above; this covers the Rust build cache specifically — 335MB of
# fully-reproducible compiler cache with zero source alongside it, never worth committing).
zerobreach-main/
_archive/zerobreach-main-dump/native-app/src-tauri/target/

# .NET build output for the native engine (Scythe.*). Note the leading slash is
# deliberately ABSENT — every one of the five projects has its own bin/ and obj/, and
# `dotnet publish` writes the single-file exe under bin/. All of it is reproducible from
# source with `dotnet build`; none of it belongs in the repo.
bin/
obj/
*.user

# OS noise
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

dist/

# Generated at release time by tools/New-IntegrityManifest.ps1 and staged into the zip.
# NOT committed: on a development tree every edit invalidates it, and engine/Phases-0.ps1
# would then report CRITICAL "signature set tampering" on every scan. Its absence is
# reported as INFO ("engine authenticity is UNVERIFIED this run"), which is the honest
# state for a dev tree.
data/integrity_manifest.json
